---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Reading SEO Strategy Examples | Campaign Plans';
const description = 'Clearly labelled SEO strategy scenarios for Reading businesses, showing campaign structure, priorities, measurement, and realistic constraints.';

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Are these case studies based on real clients?',
    a: 'No. These pages are clearly labelled strategy scenarios, not records of named or anonymised clients. They explain how a campaign could be structured for common Reading business types without presenting invented outcomes as evidence.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does an SEO plan typically take to show progress?',
    a: 'Timelines depend on the site, competitors, content, authority, and scope of work. The scenarios show an order of operations rather than a promised schedule. We set a baseline and forecast only after reviewing a real website and its search data.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you guarantee specific traffic or ranking increases?',
    a: 'No responsible SEO consultancy guarantees specific rankings. Google controls its results. We commit to a transparent process, documented work, and honest reporting against an agreed baseline.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How would you set expectations for my Reading business?',
    a: 'Expectations depend on your industry, competition, starting position, and budget. We conduct an initial audit so both parties understand the baseline, practical priorities, and measurement plan before work begins.'
  }
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://seoreading.uk/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Case Studies", "item": "https://seoreading.uk/case-studies/" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": title,
    "description": description,
    "url": "https://seoreading.uk/case-studies/",
    "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "SEO Reading", "url": "https://seoreading.uk/" },
    "breadcrumb": { "@id": "https://seoreading.uk/case-studies/#breadcrumb" }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": faqItems.map(item => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": item.q,
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": item.a }
    }))
  }
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 dot-grid-light pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="absolute -bottom-20 -left-32 w-[300px] h-[300px] rounded-full opacity-10 blur-[80px] aurora-1" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #D4AF37, transparent 70%);" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto relative z-10">
      <h1 class="fade-up">Reading SEO Strategy Examples</h1>
      <p class="subtitle fade-up" style="transition-delay: 80ms;">Illustrative campaign plans showing priorities and measurement for common Reading business types. They are not client results.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="prose fade-up">

      <p>SEO Reading publishes clearly labelled strategy scenarios showing how search campaigns can be structured for businesses across Reading and Berkshire. These pages explain the work and measurement framework without presenting fictional businesses or projected figures as client evidence.</p>

      <div class="quick-answer">
        <strong>What do these examples show?</strong> Each scenario maps a realistic sequence of technical, content, and local search work for a Reading business type. A real engagement begins with verified baseline data and reports only observed performance from the client's own analytics and search accounts.
      </div>

      <h2>Our Approach to Measurement</h2>

      <p>Real SEO campaigns should be tracked against an agreed baseline using organic clicks, qualified rankings, Google Business Profile interactions, and conversions. The examples on this page do not claim client outcomes. In live engagements, performance figures should come from the client's Google Search Console, analytics, call tracking, and lead records.</p>

      <p>Transparency is central to how we operate. These scenarios present the strategy, likely constraints, and measurement approach behind a campaign. SEO combines technical optimisation, useful content, and relevant authority signals within the competitive markets Reading businesses operate in.</p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
        <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="mt-0">Reading Law Firm SEO Growth Plan</h3>
          <p>An illustrative scenario showing how technical remediation, practice-area content, and local optimisation could be prioritised for a law firm near Forbury Square.</p>
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand">Includes: baseline, work sequence, and KPIs</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/reading-law-firm-organic-growth/">Read the strategy scenario &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="mt-0">Caversham Estate Agent Local SEO Plan</h3>
          <p>An illustrative scenario showing how Google Business Profile work, local citations, reviews, and area content could be prioritised for an independent estate agent.</p>
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand">Includes: local baseline, work sequence, and KPIs</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/caversham-estate-agent-google-maps-dominance/">Read the strategy scenario &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What Makes Reading Businesses Different for SEO</h2>

      <p>Reading sits at the centre of the Thames Valley, one of the most commercially dense corridors outside London. This creates a specific set of SEO challenges that generic agencies often overlook. Reading businesses compete not only against one another but against London firms targeting Berkshire remotely, national chains with substantial domain authority, and aggregator sites like Rightmove, Checkatrade, and Bark that dominate many local search results.</p>

      <p>The opportunity lies in Reading's geography. The town serves a catchment spanning Caversham and Emmer Green to the north, Tilehurst and Calcot to the west, Earley and Woodley to the east, and out to Wokingham, Bracknell, and Newbury. A properly structured local SEO campaign captures search demand across all of these areas from a single website. Most Reading businesses leave this multi-area visibility entirely unrealised.</p>

      <p>Reading's business park clusters also create distinctive B2B search dynamics. Green Park and Thames Valley Park house major corporate headquarters. Forbury Square is the professional services hub. Each cluster generates distinct search patterns that a locally embedded SEO consultancy understands instinctively but a remote agency would require months to learn.</p>

      <p>The businesses that invest in local SEO early gain a compounding advantage. Rankings build authority over time. Review profiles strengthen. Citation networks expand. The longer one delays, the more ground competitors gain and the harder it becomes to close the gap.</p>

      <div class="cta-box">
        <h2>Find Out Where You Stand</h2>
        <p class="text-white/90 mb-4">Request a free SEO audit and we will show you precisely where your Reading business ranks, what is holding you back, and what opportunities you are missing. No commitment, no obligation.</p>
        <a href="/free-seo-audit-reading/">Book a Consultation</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      {faqItems.map(item => (
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">{item.q}</h3>
          <p>{item.a}</p>
        </div>
      ))}

      <p>Ready to explore what SEO can accomplish for your business? Review our <a href="/services/">full range of SEO services</a> or request a <a href="/seo-audit-reading/">comprehensive SEO audit</a>. Learn more about <a href="/">SEO Reading</a> and how we help Berkshire businesses grow through organic search.</p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
